AB  - Secure transmission of medical images is critical in telemedicine and healthcare applications, where privacy and data integrity are paramount. This paper presents a hybrid approach that combines Convolutional Neural Networks (CNNs) with chaotic-map-based feature scrambling and homomorphic encryption to enhance the security of medical image transmission. In the proposed system, CNN is employed to extract robust image features, which are then secured using a chaotic map before encryption, providing dual-layer protection against unauthorized access. The effectiveness of the method is evaluated using Peak Signal-to-Noise Ratio (PSNR) to assess image quality preservation, Structural Similarity Index Measure (SSIM) to assess structural fidelity, and Encryption Speed to assess computational efficiency. Experimental results demonstrate that the hybrid approach achieves high security, preserves image quality, and maintains efficient encryption performance, enabling efficient deployment in healthcare systems. By integrating deep learning-based feature extraction, chaotic scrambling, and Homomorphic Encryption, this work presents a robust and privacy-preserving framework for secure medical image transmission.
ER  - 

