AB  - The rapid expansion of Internet of Things (IoT) in the healthcare sector has transformed the gathering, managing, and analysis of patient data; but it also presents privacy and security concerns due to the increased vulnerability to cyber-attacks. Federated Learning (FL) is a potential solution that enhances data privacy by enabling collaborative model training across different devices without disclosing the raw data. This study explores FL as a privacy-preserving strategy alongside Differential Privacy, Homomorphic Encryption, and Secure Multi-Party Computation. It discusses security and privacy challenges in IoT healthcare, use cases of FL, and dataset information in the healthcare domain. In addition, points out possible future directions to further improve security, scalability, and model performance while drawing inferences about the current stage of FL adoption in IoT healthcare.
