AB  - Vector similarity search is a cornerstone of modern applications in machine learning, information retrieval, and recommendation systems, where identifying the most similar vectors to a query is critical. [10] However, when dealing with sensitive data, ensuring privacy during the search process becomes a significant challenge. This paper presents a framework for Privacy-Preserving Vector Similarity Search using Homomorphic Encryption (HE), enabling secure computation while keeping the data and queries confidential.We leverage the K-Nearest Neighbors (K-NN) algorithm to efficiently retrieve the most relevant vectors, with computations performed directly on encrypted data. By employing homomorphic encryption, we ensure that neither the data owner nor the querying party gains access to the plaintext vectors or query. We address key challenges, including encryption overhead, efficient computation of similarity metrics such as cosine similarity or Euclidean distance in encrypted space, and scalability to high-dimensional data. We analyze a variety of distance functions while evaluating their compatibility with homomorphic encryption.Our experimental results demonstrate that the proposed framework achieves over 90% retrieval accuracy on benchmark datasets, with computation times within practical limits for moderate-dimensional vectors (up to 128 dimensions), thereby validating the feasibility of privacy-preserving similarity search. These findings provide practical insights into designing secure systems while highlighting the unique challenges associated with computation overhead in encrypted domains.This work serves as a foundation for future studies on improving the computational performance of privacy-preserving algorithms. It bridges the gap between secure computation and practical vector similarity search, paving the way for privacy-preserving applications in healthcare, finance, and other sensitive domains.
ER  - 

