AB  - The exponential growth of Big Data demands advanced cloud security mechanisms that adapt to emerging cyber threats and ensure efficient data retrieval. Traditional centralized architectures and static encryption strategies struggle against modern attack vectors and scalability challenges. This paper proposes an intelligent cloud security framework integrating AI-driven sensitivity classification, quantum-resistant and adaptive encryption, blockchain-based key management, and multi-cloud redundancy. Homomorphic encryption enables privacy-preserving computation, while an AI-based encrypted search engine enhances secure data retrieval. Extensive simulations across finance, healthcare, and government datasets demonstrate improvements in encryption speed (35 %), storage efficiency (40 %), threat mitigation (28 %), and retrieval time (50 %). The proposed system offers a robust, scalable, and future-ready solution for securing Big Data storage in cloud ecosystems.
